/**
\defgroup Fts_ftc_config_ext FrameTransform: possibile server-client configurations with external devices
\ingroup dev_tutorials

\tableofcontents

\section Fts_ftc_config_intro Description
\ref FrameTransformServer and \ref FrameTransformClient with externals devices, comes new client/server coupling configurations. In order to facilitate
the use of these new devices, here is a complete list of the allowed combinations.

\section fts_full_ros fts_full_ros compatible configurations
In the following configurations the communication with ROS/ROS2 is managed by the server. These configurations are
particularly useful when all the clients that are going to connect to the server need to have access to the transform
published on ROS/ROS2 topics

- **ftc_yarp_only** In this configurations, the client can set and get frame transforms stored in the server
\zoomimage{fts_full_ros_n_ftc_yarp_only.svg, ftc_yarp_only}

- **ftc_pub_yarp_only** In this configurations, the client can only set frame transforms stored in the server
\zoomimage{fts_full_ros_n_ftc_pub_yarp_only.svg, ftc_pub_yarp_only}

- **ftc_sub_yarp_only** In this configurations, the client can only get frame transforms stored in the server
\zoomimage{fts_full_ros_n_ftc_sub_yarp_only.svg, ftc_sub_yarp_only}
.

\section ftc_full_ros ftc_full_ros compatible configurations
In the following configurations the communication with ROS/ROS2 is managed by the client. These are particolarly useful when the server and other clients are
running on machines with no ROS/ROS2 support but need the TFs generated by those middlewares

- **ftc_full_ros** In this configurations, the client can set and get frame transforms stored in the server and also
the ones published on ROS/ROS2 topics
\zoomimage{fts_yarp_only_n_ftc_full_ros.svg, ftc_full_ros}
.

\section ftc_only_ros ftc_only_ros compatible configurations
In the following configurations, the client will only communicate with ROS/ROS2 TF topics. These configurations are useful when a YARP client has to interface with a ROS/ROS2 only system and
needs to get and set TFs from/to ROS/ROS2 topics

- **ftc_pub_ros** In this configurations, the client can only publish frame transforms to ROS/ROS2 topics
\zoomimage{ftc_ros12_pub.svg, ftc_pub_ros}

- **ftc_sub_ros** In this configurations, the client can only subscribe to frame transforms from ROS/ROS2 topics
\zoomimage{ftc_ros12_sub.svg, ftc_sub_ros}

- **ftc_full_ros** In this configurations, the client can set and get frame transforms from/to ROS/ROS2 topics
\zoomimage{ftc_ros12.svg, ftc_full_ros}
.
*/
